## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-account enforcement, not just configuration. Evaluates orchestration of SCPs, KMS, bucket policies, VPC endpoints, and automated validation.

## Key Concepts
- Organization SCPs and service control scope
- IAM boundaries and cross-account KMS key policies
- S3 bucket policy with encryption/TLS requirements
- VPC Endpoints/PrivateLink hardening
- AWS Config rules, drift detection, automated remediation

## Code Example
```javascript
// AWS SDK v3 check example
import { S3Client, GetBucketEncryptionCommand } from "@aws-sdk/client-s3";
const client = new S3Client({ region: "us-east-1" });
async function checkEncryption(bucket) {
  try {
    const res = await client.send(new GetBucketEncryptionCommand({ Bucket: bucket }));
    console.log("Encryption:", res.ServerSideEncryptionConfiguration);
  } catch (err) {
    console.error("No encryption configured", err);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test SCP compliance across accounts without affecting existing buckets?
- How would you handle CMK rotation and tenant access during key updates?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of least privilege, data security in transit/at rest, cross-account auditing, and implementing simple defense-in-depth for a common ingestion pattern.

## Key Concepts
- Presigned URLs, Lambda IAM, S3 bucket policies
- SSE-KMS and CMK rotation
- S3 Object Lock and immutable logs
- CloudTrail integration
- Input validation (Content-Type, size)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Lambda presigned URL generator outline
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const s3 = new AWS.S3();
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const {filename, contentType, size}=JSON.parse(event.body);
  if (!contentType.startsWith('image/') || size>5*1024*1024) throw new Error('Invalid');
  const url = s3.getSignedUrl('putObject', {Bucket:'image-upload-bucket',Key:filename,ContentType:contentType,Expires:300});
  return {statusCode:200, body: JSON.stringify({url})};
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate the CMK and rotate keys used in the bucket policy without breaking existing uploads?
- What logging verifications would you run to confirm immutability and no unauthorized uses?

